{"id":5910,"date":"2022-03-02T13:59:40","date_gmt":"2022-03-02T21:59:40","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=5910"},"modified":"2025-10-23T13:40:16","modified_gmt":"2025-10-23T20:40:16","slug":"3-5-height-sensor-cde-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/3-5-height-sensor-cde-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"3.5: Bottom Range (Height) Sensor"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22137c93270\" name=\"6a22137c93270\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>We've Moved!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1761252013359{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-11766\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"81\" height=\"82\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: <a href=\"http:\/\/learn.robolink.com\">Robolink Learn<\/a>! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June 2026. This version of Basecamp will no longer be updated and uses outdated references to Blockly for Robolink. You can access the previous version of <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22137c933a6\" name=\"6a22137c933a6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Goals and Steps to Success<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<p class=\"\" data-source-line=\"5\">The goals for this lesson are:<\/p>\n<ol data-source-line=\"7\">\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"7\">Understand how the\u00a0<strong><code>get_height()<\/code><\/strong>\u00a0function simplifies calculations.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"8\">Learn how the drone uses barometer values to measure height.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"9\">Use\u00a0<strong><code>get_height()<\/code><\/strong>\u00a0at different points in a program.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"10\">Store the drone&#8217;s height as a variable and make decisions with it.<\/li>\n<li class=\"highlight-line\" data-source-line=\"11\">Identify differences between measured height and actual height.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"12\">Explore why program height might differ from reality.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22137c93402\" name=\"6a22137c93402\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>How Does the Bottom Range Sensor Work?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The bottom range sensor relies on an infrared sensor chip. Underneath your drone, you will be able to find the bottom range sensor. <em>See those two dots?<\/em> One of those emits the infrared light, and the other receives the infrared that is reflected from the surface. The chip calculates the distance based on the time it took for the infrared light to come back to the receiver.[\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]<strong>Note: The maximum range for the bottom range sensor is 1.5 meters.<\/strong>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;9443&#8243; img_size=&#8221;full&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22137c93453\" name=\"6a22137c93453\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Height Measurement Blocks<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text][\/vc_column_text][vc_column_text]In the last lesson, you learned about the barometer as a way of estimating altitude. Now, you&#8217;re going to explore measuring height using the bottom range IR height sensor. There are two functions from the &#8220;Sensors&#8221; menu that you can use. The blocks <strong><code>get_range(bottom,cm)<\/code><\/strong>\u00a0and\u00a0<strong><code>get_height()<\/code><\/strong>\u00a0will return the same values.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10611&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22137c9349e\" name=\"6a22137c9349e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Takeoff Height<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<em>What is the average takeoff height for CoDrone EDU?<\/em> Find out by running a test. Build a program that takes off, prints the height, then lands.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10612&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Now, run the experiment 5 times. Record the height for each time. <em>What is the average? Does it change depending on the battery level?<\/em>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22137c934e7\" name=\"6a22137c934e7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Measuring Height in a Loop<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]You can use the\u00a0<strong><code>get_height()<\/code><\/strong>\u00a0function in a loop to measure height repeatedly. Start with a takeoff and set the\u00a0<strong><code>throttle<\/code><\/strong>\u00a0variable to 20. Fly up for one second and take a height reading. Repeat for a total of 3 times.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10613&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22137c935d3\" name=\"6a22137c935d3\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Fly to Height<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<p class=\"\" data-source-line=\"42\">The height sensor can also be used to control throttle. In this program, CoDrone EDU will take off and rise up to a 1 meter (100cm). Here are the steps.<\/p>\n<ol data-source-line=\"44\">\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"44\">Create a variable called\u00a0<code>max_height<\/code>\u00a0and set it to 100 (this will be in centimeters).<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"45\">Takeoff and set throttle to 20.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"46\">Use the height sensor to read the height in centimeters and store it in a variable called\u00a0<code>current_height<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"47\">In a while loop, move up while\u00a0<code>current_height<\/code>\u00a0returns a value less than max_height.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"48\">Update\u00a0<code>current_height<\/code>\u00a0by taking another reading of the height sensor.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"49\">Print the value of\u00a0<code>current_height<\/code>.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"50\">Add a land outside the loop.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p class=\"highlight-line highlight-active\" data-source-line=\"52\">Run the code. <em>Does the drone stop flying up at 100cm?<\/em> You might notice some print statements return 999.9. Let&#8217;s improve the code in the next step.<\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12935&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22137c936a6\" name=\"6a22137c936a6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Improving the Program<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Sometimes the height sensor will return a reading of 999.9 if the sensor was not able to retrieve a value or if there was an error. Fortunately, we can improve the code to account for this scenario. A sensor value of 999.9 is an error, so CoDrone EDU should continue to throttle up. To do this, we will add an <code>or<\/code> statement to the conditional. From the &#8220;Logic&#8221; menu, select the <strong>logical operators<\/strong> block.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12696&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]Use the dropdown menu to change the operator to\u00a0<code>or<\/code>. Then, temporarily remove your original conditional statement and replace it with this one.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12937&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]The program should still keep flying if the current height has not increased past the max height. Return the original conditional to the left side of the <code>or<\/code>\u00a0statement.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12938&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<p class=\"highlight-line\" data-source-line=\"70\">Finally, the program should also check if the height sensor returned an error. In other words, if the height sensor is below the maximum height OR the height was above 999 (an error), keep flying. Fill in the rest of the conditional and test your program.<\/p>\n<div class=\"absolute top-0 right-0 select-none floating-action flex flex-col items-end z-[60]\">\n<div class=\"flex flex-row items-center\">\n<div class=\"ml-1 flex\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;12939&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]You learned how to combine if statements to check and ignore any height sensor data that may not be useful for your program.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22137c9375b\" name=\"6a22137c9375b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 9<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge 1: Fact Checker<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<p class=\"\" data-source-line=\"78\"><em>You have been using the height sensor to fly to various heights, but how accurate is it?<\/em> For this challenge, you will create a relationship between the actual height of the drone and the data returned from the IR sensor. Grab a partner for this activity to take measurements more easily. Here are the steps:<\/p>\n<ul data-source-line=\"80\">\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"80\">In a forever loop, write code that will print the height sensor data when the space bar is pressed<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"81\">In the loop, after each keyboard press, use a <strong><code>sleep()<\/code><\/strong>function for 0.5 seconds to delay the key press for the next measurement.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"82\">Find a ruler or measuring tape to use for measuring the drone&#8217;s height. This is easier with a partner so that they can hold the measuring tape for you.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"83\">Run your program so that it&#8217;s ready to receive key press commands.<\/li>\n<li class=\"\" data-source-line=\"84\">Move the drone with your hand to various heights. For example, measure 6 inches off the ground, 12 inches, 18 inches, etc. Press the space bar at each reading and record the result.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p class=\"highlight-line\" data-source-line=\"86\">Finally, analyze the results.<em> How sensitive is the height sensor? Does it change based on the flooring?<\/em> Remember that the height sensor relies on infrared light to make its measurements. If light cannot reflect well off the surface, you may get an incorrect or inaccurate reading.<\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7756&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a22137c937b7\" name=\"6a22137c937b7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 10<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Lesson Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<div>\n<div>Congratulations! With the CoDrone EDU&#8217;s height sensor, you&#8217;ve learned to measure the drone&#8217;s current height and save that information. In the next lesson, you will learn how to use the same technology to avoid obstacles.<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7547&#8243; img_size=&#8221;750&#215;670&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 11 We've Moved! [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1761252013359{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: Robolink Learn! Lessons here&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/3-5-height-sensor-cde-blockly\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4742,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3877,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1782,1848,1770,1793,1826,1482,853,694,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2195,2159,2108,4328,14401,2160,2122,2155],"class_list":["post-5910","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-advanced","lesson-tag-barometer","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-height","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-sensor","module-advanced","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/5910","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":32,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/5910\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13635,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/5910\/revisions\/13635"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/4742"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=5910"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=5910"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=5910"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}